Independent check of the retained rank three theorem
====================================================

The existing rank_three_intersections.tex proves the full intersection
property for a finite nonabelian simple group generated by three nonidentity
involutions a,b,c with a and c distinct and commuting. The argument is sound.
This is a review of that retained theorem, not a replacement theorem or a
novelty claim. Its Leemans--Mulpas citation supports the definitions; this
review does not attribute the exact elementary proof to that publication.

Root's shorter proof is also valid. Degenerate adjacent pairs cannot occur:
if a=b or b=c, generation is dihedral; if an adjacent pair commutes, an
endpoint is central. Thus each D1=<a,b>, D2=<b,c> has a cyclic rotation
subgroup C1=<ab>, C2=<bc> of index two, with b outside both. For T=C1∩C2,
cyclicity makes T characteristic in each Ci and hence normal in each Di.
Since the Di generate G, T is cyclic normal in G, so simplicity gives T=1.
No normality of D1∩D2 in either Di is assumed.

The two parity maps embed H=D1∩D2 in C2×C2, with b of parity(1,1).
Thus H=<b> or H is a Klein four group. In the latter case its unique
nontrivial h in C1 and k in C2 are distinct and b=hk. Each order-two
rotation is central in its own Di. The groups U=<a,k> and V=<c,h> commute,
because all four cross-generator pairs commute, and UV=G. Each is generated
by two involutions and is solvable, so G would be solvable. Alternatively,
U is nontrivial normal in G; simplicity gives U=G and V≤Z(G)=1, contradicting
c≠1. Both contradictions allow degenerate auxiliary dihedral factors.
Consequently D1∩D2=<b>.

The third maximal parabolic is <a,c>=V4. A larger intersection with D1
than <a> would contain c and make G=D1 dihedral; similarly its intersection
with D2 is <c>. No generator is in the opposite pair-generated subgroup,
and distinct singleton parabolics intersect trivially. These identities,
together with nested, empty and full cases, exhaust all subset pairs and
prove the full rank three intersection property.

For the actual Fi22 application the named simple G, membership and middle
involution meanings remain imported. The retained endpoint decoder checks
nonidentity involutions a,c, their distinctness and commutation on the
whole action. It does not newly prove that the virtual middle product b
is an involution: that is the original GLOBAL class/two-fibre identification
premise. The same accepted seed, normal-G-in-A and exact word/action joins
put all three marks in G. The strict eleven/thirteen criterion proves
R=<ab,bc>=G inside this G. Since R≤<a,b,c>≤G, the marking generates G and
the retained theorem applies. No additional point or group calculation is
needed for this mathematical composition.

